The Sparse-IDCS implementation adapts the IDCS project by Shiran Levy and
collaborators (https://github.com/ShiLevy/IDCS). The upstream modules in
vendor/idcs_original are provided under the upstream GNU GPL version 3
license and are used only on their linear straight-ray path. This repository
is distributed under GPL-3.0-only; see LICENSE.

The straight-ray kernel retains its original author attribution to E. Laloy.
The source image embedded into the experiment scripts derives from the
binary-channels channels.npy used by the IDCS example and attributed to
Zahner et al. (2016). The embedded bits are exact source-image crops, not
previous reconstruction results.

No field measurements or field-validation experiment are distributed here.
